Z||000000||fyerstarter||06-04-2001||01:26 PM||||Well **** , I started up this morning and drove about a mile and all of a sudden the temp gage rocketed into the red. I pulled over and coolant was bubbling out of the overflow. Popped the cap and there's oil in there. Let it cool down and putted it home. Now car runs like **** . <P>Does this sound to you guys like a head gasket? Is there anything else besides this that can cause that to happen? Aside from a cracked head :\<P>Oh, does anyone have a ballpark estimate on how much a shop would charge in the US, Southern California to be exact to fix it? <P>Is there any way to tell which head is the problem without taking them both off?<P>Thanks guys. What a morning :[||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||06-04-2001||01:34 PM||||Compression test will tell you wich one let go most of the time. You may as well replace both while it's appart. It's only a little more work than doing one at that point. Check the valve wear and valve seals as well.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 06-04-2001).]||||reg||1
